Defend the selection, service and recovery account (@mat-selection-review: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @materials-engineering, #materials-engineering "../research/Connect-material-state-model-and-observation.lingua#r_6BM5Z0CF2SCAW4X4405N8YZNDZ") { r_3EKGFH7N9TS7SSRZHCP0MX6E8W
**Read:** Complete all three investigations and the substantial readings. Revisit structure, kinetics, response, processing and deterioration wherever the choice assumes an unexplained material state.

Derive selection indices from actual constraints and geometry freedoms; reconcile property sources; compare multiple constraints and objectives; and explain uncertainty and qualification. Follow accepted production, service observations, failure, repair, reuse and constituent recovery. Defend a life-cycle comparison with functional equivalence, boundaries, inventory, allocation, timing and sensitivity.

**Demonstrate:** Reproduce the beam comparison independently and explain why a favorable isolated property can lose under complete requirements. Defend the three studies against alternative assumptions and revise them. State the work and information needed to preserve useful material performance across transfers.

Continue into multiscale models, integrated process-to-service investigations and independent materials research. Carry the selection and service questions into the interpretation of primary evidence.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).

**Continue in materials engineering:** [Connect material state, model and observation](../research/Connect-material-state-model-and-observation.lingua#r_6BM5Z0CF2SCAW4X4405N8YZNDZ).

